From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: rtl8365mb: prepare an inactive NCTL host-mode experiment

Prepare an experimental host-managed NCTL setup primitive for the AX55 Pro
switch, restricted to the family-D 0x6642/0x0050 register layout.

Disable the NCTL engine using the same register as the existing family-D
SerDes pause helper, and verify that it reads back disabled. Serialize the
write and readback with all indirect SerDes transactions. Subsequent
pause/restore transactions observe zero and must not restart the engine.
Report every failure and return an error if the disable does not stick.
Do not restore an unknown program after a failed preparation.

OpenWrt PR #19644 contains a host-managed SerDes approach for family D,
including receiver re-latching, but targets revision 0x0010 with its CPU
on port 6. That is not evidence that the program can be omitted on the
Pro's revision 0x0050 with CPU port 7 and two HSGMII lanes. Do not copy
its family-C DW8051 reset handling onto the distinct NCTL engine.

This helper is deliberately uncalled. It neither uploads firmware nor
establishes NCTL quiescence timing, receiver re-latching, cold-boot
initialization or working links. Do not register family D or add an
automatic firmware-to-host fallback. A serial/RAM-boot experiment must
validate both lanes and frame transfer before making this path active.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/19644
Signed-off-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
@@ -1310,5 +1310,43 @@
 }
 
+/* Experimental only: callers must not assume a disabled NCTL is sufficient
+ * to initialize either SerDes. Keep this uncalled until hardware validation.
+ */
+static int __maybe_unused rtl8367d_nctl_host_prepare(struct realtek_priv *priv)
+{
+	struct rtl8365mb *mb = priv->chip_data;
+	u32 nctl;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (mb->chip_info->mac_force_layout != RTL8365MB_MAC_FORCE_D ||
+	    mb->chip_info->chip_id != 0x6642 ||
+	    mb->chip_info->chip_ver != 0x0050) {
+		dev_err(priv->dev, "unsupported family-D NCTL host-mode revision\n");
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	}
+
+	rtl83xx_lock(priv);
+	ret = regmap_write(priv->map_nolock, RTL8367D_NCTL_EN_REG, 0);
+	if (ret)
+		goto out;
+
+	ret = regmap_read(priv->map_nolock, RTL8367D_NCTL_EN_REG, &nctl);
+	if (ret)
+		goto out;
+	if (nctl) {
+		dev_err(priv->dev, "NCTL remains enabled: %#x\n", nctl);
+		ret = -EIO;
+	}
+
+out:
+	rtl83xx_unlock(priv);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(priv->dev, "failed to prepare NCTL host mode: %pe\n",
+			ERR_PTR(ret));
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 static int rtl8367d_sds_selector(struct realtek_priv *priv,
 				 const struct rtl8365mb_extint *extint)
 {
